hairiokuilo-by-luminaire for Debian
----------------------------------

The intro was released as a self-extracting shell script
(hairiokuilu_by_luminaire.sh). The executable has been unpacked and
renamed.

The binary was also patched to remove fullscreen (SDL 1.2 breaks the
display). This patch is already in the orig tarball.

At build time, debian/patch-binary.pl patches a copy of the executable
(build/hairiokuilu-by-luminaire), the orig tarball is not modified:
 - the intro reused stack slots as arguments for glCompileShader(),
   glLinkProgram() and glUseProgram(). Current NVIDIA drivers overwrite
   them, glUseProgram() got a garbage id and the screen stayed white. The
   calls are rewritten, with the same size, to push their arguments again;
 - the fragment shader is replaced by debian/shader.frag, same length:
   "#version 150 compatibility" (Mesa refused the shader without
   #version), an explicit smoothstep() (reversed and equal edges are
   undefined, Mesa rendered another picture), without unused code.
   With NVIDIA, the pictures are identical to the original shader.
The script checks the original bytes before patching.

The executable is a hand-made ELF without section headers: objdump and
dpkg-shlibdeps cannot read it, so the libraries are declared by hand in
debian/control, dh_makeshlibs is skipped in debian/rules, and lintian
sees it as a statically linked binary.

executable seems to be compiled for an unknown distribution

no GCC version string left in the executable

Source files:
-------------
none (no section headers, no symbol table)

